.TH BOOTSTASH 8 "September 2026" "bootstash" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bootstash \- operator tools for bootstashd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstash
\fBcheck-config\fR
[\fB\-defaults\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
.PP
.B bootstash
\fBprovision-google\fR
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-origin\fR \fIurl\fR]
[\fB\-project\fR \fIid\fR]
[\fB\-json\fR \fIpath\fR]
.PP
.B bootstash
\fBlinks\fR
[\fB\-defaults\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
.PP
.B bootstash
\fBunlink\fR
[\fB\-defaults\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
.I user
.PP
.B bootstash
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootstash
is the operator CLI for the bootstash daemon. It does not serve HTTP or
call PAM.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check-config
Parse dist defaults
.RI ( /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist ),
.IR /etc/default/bootstash ,
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json ,
every
.B BIND
spec, and TLS files when HTTPS is on (skipped if
.BR TLS=no ).
Exit 0 if the daemon could start (missing
interfaces are not an error here). Same as
.B bootstashd \-t .
.TP
.B provision-google
Print a four-step Google console recipe (project, branding,
Web application client, download JSON) with a recommended
value at each step, including the exact OIDC redirect URI
.RB ( $PUBLIC_URL/oidc/callback ).
It says whether that URI is
.B https
(daemon would speak HTTPS: PEMs and not
.BR TLS=no ;
BIND port stays) or
.B http
(no certs, or
.BR TLS=no ),
and that finding certs does not move
.B BIND
to 443.
Then install the Web application client JSON the console
downloads as
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
.RB ( 0640
.BR root:bootstash ;
.B \-json
or a prompted path).
That file is the console
.B Download JSON
object
.RB ( web.client_id
/
.BR web.client_secret ).
Desktop
.RB ( installed )
JSON is rejected.
Reads
.B PUBLIC_URL
from
.I /etc/default/bootstash
(or
.BR \-origin ).
If unset, the same
.B CERT_NAME
or
.B hostname \-f
plus listen-port default as
.BR bootstashd
is used.
Needs root (or
.BR sudo )
to write that file; it does not write TLS certs (the Let’s Encrypt
hook does) and does not edit
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
It does
.B not
create the Google OAuth web client
.RB ( gcloud
has no API for that type).
Consent / branding is once per GCP project.
One web client per
.BR PUBLIC_URL .
If
.B gcloud
is on
.BR PATH ,
the current project id is used for console links.
It does not create Unix users.
.TP
.B links
Print each OIDC→PAM map as
.B user issuer sub
(one row per subject).
Needs read access to
.I $DATA/state
(usually
.BR sudo ).
Empty table: no rows, exit 0.
Email is not a column.
.B ADMIN_USERS
does not grant this.
.TP
.B unlink
Drop every
.B (issuer, sub)
mapped to
.I user
in
.I $DATA/state/links.json
and clear
.B pam_user
on those sessions.
The next Google sign-in for those subjects must
.B POST /link
again.
Does not delete the cubby.
v1 has no HTTP
.BR /unlink .
.B ADMIN_USERS
does not grant this; write access to
.I $DATA/state
does (usually
.BR sudo ).
Does not call PAM and does not create or delete Unix users.
Changing or disabling the Unix account does not drop the map.
State files stay owned as
.I $DATA/state
(not root) so the daemon can still read them.
.TP
.B version
Print the version from
.B git describe
(\fB\-\-version\fR,
.BR \-version ,
.B \-V
are aliases).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-defaults " path"
Dist defaults. Default:
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist .
Used by
.BR check-config ,
.BR links ,
and
.BR unlink .
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Operator config. Default:
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.TP
.BI \-secrets " path"
OIDC client secrets file. Default:
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json .
.B provision-google
writes it;
.B links
and
.B unlink
do not use OIDC keys.
.TP
.BI \-origin " url"
.B PUBLIC_URL
for
.B provision-google
when it is not already in the operator file.
.TP
.BI \-project " id"
GCP project id for
.B provision-google
console URLs when
.B gcloud
has none.
.TP
.BI \-json " path"
Downloaded Web application client JSON for
.BR provision-google .
Use
.B \-
to read stdin.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstashd (8),
.BR bootstash (5),
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/QUICKSTART.md
